This method sometimes returns fewer names than I expect, and once it threw an ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException — it's inconsistent between runs on the same input. Can you figure out why and fix it?

```java
public List<String> processNames(List<Person> people) {
    List<String> results = new ArrayList<>();
    people.parallelStream().forEach(p -> {
        if (p.isActive()) {
            results.add(p.getName().toUpperCase());
        }
    });
    return results;
}
```

Can you modernize this Java 8-style code to use modern Java streams (this is a Java 21 project), computing both the average and the count in a single pass over the orders list?

```java
public double[] computeStats(List<Order> orders) {
    double sum = 0;
    int count = 0;
    for (Order o : orders) {
        sum += o.getAmount();
        count++;
    }
    double avg = count == 0 ? 0 : sum / count;
    return new double[]{avg, count};
}
```
